": ["Replace (Gly)n with a concrete representative (e.g., diglycine, triglycine, etc.) to allow balancing.", "Clarify all product species and stoichiometry."]}, {"pathway_id": "P5", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_011": 0.5}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.5, "pathway_coherence": 0.85, "environmental_progression": 0.9, "target_achievement": 0.7, "overall_confidence": 0.69, "feedback": "Implements classical HCN/NH3/ammonium cyanide hydrolysis producing amino acids (Lowe et al., Matthews & Moser). Network treats as black-box single step, but balance fails drastically (large deficits in C, N, O, H). Mechanism is plausible as multi-step/ensemble, but not for a balanced equation to threonine. Should clarify fate of HCN and product mixture.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_011"], "suggestions": ["Indicate and balance oligomerization and hydrolysis steps.", "Treat as an ensemble process and state range of products explicitly."]}, {"pathway_id": "P6", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_012": 0.5}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.5, "pathway_coherence": 0.8, "environmental_progression": 1.0, "target_achievement": 0.7, "overall_confidence": 0.68, "feedback": "A single reaction node represents gamma radiolysis of HCN and yields threonine after hydrolysis, paralleling the Sweeney/Ponnamperuma irradiation experiments. Convenient as an abstraction, but fails mass conservation fatally as written. Mechanistic details are simplified away; better as a process node than a one-step reaction.", "approved": false, "problematic_reactions": ["rxn_012"], "suggestions": ["Expand into explicit multi-step oligomerization, radical formation, and hydrolysis (as in literature).", "Balance representative net equation or indicate ensemble process."]}, {"pathway_id": "P7", "reaction_scores": {"rxn_013": 0.6}, "chemical_feasibility": 0.65, "pathway_coherence": 0.8, "environmental_progression": 1.0, "target_achievement": 0.7, "overall_confidence": 0.74, "feedback": "Follows the archetypal Miller-Urey-Parker sp