ified. Environmental details plausible (mild aqueous). The pathway provides a credible alternative to the Strecker route but needs reaction balancing and clarification of precursor vs. free amino acid.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_005\", \"rxn_006\", \"rxn_007\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Balance HCN trimerization to aminomalononitrile (possible HCN loss as NH3, H2, or other byproducts).\",\n                \"Define stoichiometry of adduct formation and hydrolysis, add missing species.\",\n                \"Clarify endpoint as free threonine or post-hydrolysis product.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P3\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_008\": 0.62,\n                \"rxn_009\": 0.8\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.71,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.85,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.98,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.8,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.77,\n            \"feedback\": \"This pathway directly encodes Ivanov's glycine+acetaldehyde reaction. Glycine formation from HCN/NH3/H2O (rxn_008) is not fully mass-conserving per balance check, but is a well-established process experimentally. The condensation step to threonine is chemically plausible, though selectivity is low per the literature. Environmental plausibility (weakly acidic, moderately hot) is high, and target achievement is reasonable but concedes significant product mixture.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_008\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Correct glycine synthesis balance (may need to specify intermediates and missing small-molecule byproducts explicitly).\",\n                \"Note threo/allothreo diastereomer and racemic mixture formation.\",\n                \"Indicate post-synthetic purification issues or follow Ivanov's product analysis.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P4\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_008\": 0.62,\n                \"rxn_010\": 0.77\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.7,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.8,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.96,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.77,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.75,\n            \"feedback\": \"Oligoglycine + acetaldehyde condensation route is analogous to P3 but invokes peptide intermediates; chemical precedent is valid but issues with specificity, mixture complexity and correct balancing (glycine formation). Low selectivity, product mixture likely as in Ivanov study.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_008\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Tighten stoichiometry on glycine/oligoglycine formation.\",\n                \"Clarify nature/ratio of threonine within overall amino acid mixture.\",\n                \"Provide evidence for the extent of oligomer conversion.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P5\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_011\": 0.55\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.55,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.75,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.87,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.80,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.68,\n            \"feedback\": \"Bulk HCN/NH3 polymer hydrolysis is a valid representation of the Matthews & Moser class of experiments. However, this is the most unbalanced reaction per RDKit and mass conservation is poor; the threonine is yielded in hydrolysates as a very minor component, with complex polymeric intermediates. Mechanistically, this pathway is best depicted as a network ensemble rather than a single reaction.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_011\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Acknowledge/treat as an ensemble process, not a single-step reaction.\",\n                \"Clarify the nature of the precursor intermediate and yield.\",\n                \"Attempt to construct a broader mechanistic map if possible.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P6\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_012\": 0.55\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.57,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.78,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.90,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.77,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.67,\n            \"feedback\": \"Gamma radiolysis of HCN (Sweeney et al.) accurately reproduces formation of hydrolysable threonine. The step is properly listed as unbalanced, consistent with the network-wide issue of ensemble vs. single-reaction representation. Side product mixtures and ambiguous intermediates should be explicitly noted.\",\n            \"approved\": false,\n            \"problematic_reactions\": [\"rxn_012\"],\n            \"suggestions\": [\n                \"Frame as an ensemble/oligomerization process with hydrolysis, not as a single reaction.\",\n                \"Cite actual yields and discuss radiolytic dose-dependent product distribution.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"pathway_id\": \"P7\",\n            \"reaction_scores\": {\n                \"rxn_013\": 0.6\n            },\n            \"chemical_feasibility\": 0.63,\n            \"pathway_coherence\": 0.77,\n            \"environmental_progression\": 0.84,\n            \"target_achievement\": 0.79,\n            \"overall_confidence\": 0.67,\n            \"feedback\": \"Miller-type H2S-rich spark discharge is supported by direct experiment (Parker et al.). Reaction is unbalanced per element/charge conservation. Actual pathway from feedstocks to threonine remains undefined, as expe