istry of PAH/H2O/NH3 ice", "inputs": ["mol_003", "mol_011"], "outputs": ["mol_014"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "15K", "pressure": "low vacuum", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": false, "other": "UV/EUV irradiation"}, "mechanism": "Photo-induced radical chemistry in mixed PAH/H2O/NH3 ices produces complex organic residues from which threonine emerges after workup.", "reasoning": "Chen et al., 2008. Demonstrates threonine among hydrolysis products of ice residues."}, {"id": "rxn_017", "name": "Ice-organic residue hydrolysis to free threonine", "inputs": ["mol_014", "mol_011"], "outputs": ["mol_008"], "environment": "Biochemical", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "340K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": "Strong acid hydrolysis"}, "mechanism": "Acidic hydrolysis of complex ice organic residue releases free threonine and other amino acids.", "reasoning": "Elsila et al., 2007; Chen et al., 2008. Threonine detected in posthydrolysis mixture."}, {"id": "rxn_018", "name": "Interstellar radical recombination to lactaldehyde", "inputs": ["mol_017", "mol_018"], "outputs": ["mol_006"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "5K (interstellar ice)", "pressure": "ultra-high vacuum", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": false, "other": "Energetic electron irradiation"}, "mechanism": "Radical\u2013radical recombination between formyl and 1-hydroxyethyl radical yields lactaldehyde in cold CO/EtOH ices.", "reasoning": "Wang et al., 2024. Mechanistically clean, fully balanced; this lactaldehyde enters established Strecker chemistry for threonine."}, {"id": "rxn_019", "name": "Formyl radical generation from CO", "inputs": ["mol_015"], "outputs": ["mol_017"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "5K", "pressure": "ultra-high vacuum", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": false, "other": "Energetic electron irradiation"}, "mechanism": "CO undergoes electron-induced fragmentation to yield formyl radical.", "reasoning": "Wang et al., 2024; direct radical source for ice pathway."}, {"id": "rxn_020", "name": "1-hydroxyethyl radical generation from ethanol", "inputs": ["mol_016"], "outputs": ["mol_018"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "5K", "pressure": "ultra-high vacuum", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": false, "other": "Energetic electron irradiation"}, "mechanism": "Ethanol undergoes electron-induced \u03b1-cleavage to generate 1-hydroxyethyl radical.", "reasoning": "Wang et al., 2024; direct mechanistic source for radical recombination step."}, {"id": "rxn_021", "name": "Proposed CGP (Complex Glycine Precursor) alkylation with acetaldehyde", "inputs": ["mol_010", "mol_001"], "outputs": ["mol_008"], "environment": "Surface", "agents": [null], "conditions": {"temperature": "340\u2013350K", "pressure": "1 atm", "catalyst": null, "aqueous": true, "other": "Hydrothermal or acidic aqueous"}, "mechanism": "Speculative prebiotic alkylation of a polymeric glycine precursor with acetaldehyde yields threonine.", "reasoning": "Kuroda & Kobayashi, 2024. Not yet experimentally demonstrated for threonine; included as a plausible network edge."}], "pathways": [{"pathway_id": "P1", "name": "Cyanosulfidic (Kiliani\u2013Fischer\u2013Strecker) lactaldehyde route", "description": "HCN-derived acetaldehyde is converted to lactonitrile, which is photoreduced to lactaldehyde, and enters Strecker chemistry yielding threonine aminonitrile, then hydrolyzed to threonine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_001", "rxn_002", "rxn_003", "rxn_004"], "key_intermediates": ["mol_004", "mol_006", "mol_007"]}, {"pathway_id": "P2", "name": "Aminomalononitrile + acetaldehyde route", "description": "HCN trimerizes to aminomalononitrile, which alkylates with acetaldehyde, yielding aminonitrile, and is hydrolyzed and decarboxylated to threonine.", "reaction_sequence": ["rxn_005", "rxn_006", "rxn_007"], "key_intermedia